Send $z_1,z_2,z_3$ to $0,1,oo$ by a Möbius transformation $alpha$. If the four points lie on a circle, circle preservation sends their circle to the unique circle through $0,1,oo$, namely $RR_oo$, so $alpha(z_4)$ is real or infinity. Conversely, if $alpha(z_4) in RR_oo$, then $0,1,oo,alpha(z_4)$ lie on $RR_oo$, and circle preservation carries this circle back to one containing the original four points.
